out --by-customer, aging prints exactly what it \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mprints today. If you have built something different already, change it to this.\u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mThought for \u001b[1m9s\u001b[22m \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m Approved criteria noted. Let me look at the existing tests to match conventions, then\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  write the FB-112 tests before touching the code.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m●\u001b[39m Reading tests/parse.test.ts\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  tests/parse.test.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;180mHashing…\u001b[13G\u001b[38;5;246m11s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m3.1k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
