[0.033,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mI called Marta. These are the criteria for FB-112, approved: 1. \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging <file> \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153m--by-customer\u001b[38;5;231m prints one row per customer who has overdue invoices: the customer's \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mname, what they owe in each bucket (1-30, 31-60, 61-90, over 90 days) and their total \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231moverdue. 2. The customer with the largest total overdue comes first. 3. A customer with\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mnothing overdue is not listed. 4. Without --by-customer, aging prints exactly what it \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mprints today. If you have built something different already, change it to this.\u001b[39m         \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;246mThought\u001b[15G\u001b[1m9s\u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m Approved criteria noted. Let me look at the existing tests to match conventions, then\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  write the FB-112 tests before touching the code.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m●\u001b[39m Reading tests/parse.test.ts\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[39m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mNow write tests. I'll add to tests/aging.test.ts. I need to decide the API to test \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3magainst. The tests are part of the approved criteria implementation, but the exact \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m\u001b[3mAPI is my design. I'll test \u001b[38;5;153magingByCustomer\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;5;153mrenderAging\u001b[39m/\u001b[38;5;153mrenderAgingByCustomer\u001b[39m? \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m   \u001b[2m\u001b[3mCriterion 4 is \"Without --by-customer, aging prints exactly what it prints today.\" \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BBest to test the CLI? Or test 